  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "At Iron Eagle blessed land he mocks Nu Er Gu for looking pathetic after fighting iron crown eagles, then refuses to charge in the same way. Narration places him as not weaker than Nu Er Gu: Nu Er Gu cultivates sound path for Nu Er tribe, while Guan Chou cultivates transformation path for Guan tribe, and both have equally strong Huang Jin backgrounds. He Ruo treats their presence near the eagles as proof that ground resources are mostly already taken.",
      "chapters": [
        1107
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_iron_eagle_blessed_land",
        "char_nu_er_gu",
        "fac_nu_er_tribe",
        "fac_guan_tribe",
        "char_he_ruo"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He is over eight feet tall. He has bright red pupils, dark blue skin, purple hair, and sharp fangs.",
      "chapters": [
        1107
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "When Hei Tie Sheng engages the invaders, Guan Chou has turned into a lion and roars as he crashes into him. The lion flies out like a rag doll. Charged again, Guan Chou screeches, turns into a little bird, and flies away. Hei Tie Sheng calls him a coward and cannot catch up.",
      "chapters": [
        1109
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "lion-and-bird-forms",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_hei_tie_sheng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At the blood battle martial competition, talk places Nu Er Gu’s battle strength at the same level as Guan Chou of Guan tribe, Unfettered Scholar, and Pi Shui Han.",
      "chapters": [
        1193
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
